WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:07.600
A bell of awakening tolls and the
unkindled rises from his grave in the Cemetery of Ash.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.140
Welcome, everyone, to Dark Souls 3.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:17.960
In this episode we're going to be taking out the Ashen
Judge, exploring the new Firelink Shrine

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:25.160
and once again fighting through the Highwall of Lothric, except this time a new boss awaits

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:30.340
We start to explore, killing
all the scattered hollows that litter the graveyard

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.080
and the first item we pick
up is the Ashen Estus Flask on a corpse

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.450
of an elite knight which is surely a nod to Oscar, right? he was leaning on

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.480
He was leaning on something that looks suspiciously like a Lord Vessel.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.820
There are actually three Lord vessel-like polls in this episode alone, so

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.620
see if you can spot them.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.280
A bit of a challenge for you.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.780
And then there's
this message: "pull back"

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.620
and as soon as you read this you're like:

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.100
"Oh, shit! I gotta go back!"

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:05.740
"This isn't safe. What if there's an Asylum Demon down here or an Ogre guarding treasure..."

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.140
"...or a giant Crystal Lizard that drops an incredibly valuable scale?"

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.320
These lizards are back with a vengeance.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.360
I feel like finally they've evolved 
to a more dangerous state and

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.720
are getting revenge for all their children that you've been killing in the past few games.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.080
That's my headcanon for at least.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.500
In terms of real story, their scale description says that:

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:34.060
"In rare cases crystal lizards devour souls, 
growing to monstrous proportions."

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.620
And you might be noticing:

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.960
"That short bow is a little bit 
better than it used to be, right?"

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.580
And it is. 
I really like this playstyle where you

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:47.700
fall back for a few fast shots and then
when they close the gap, you slash at them with

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.390
melee its proactive and varied and fun

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:55.240
and I really like the way weapon arts
are shaping up so far.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.340
We use this same technique really soon 
against the boss of the tutorial

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.240
but first let's admire a few things:

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:08.280
First up, this 'arrow dodge', hit
detections are pretty on point.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.140
And second: these views.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.300
This build is running
on PS4 and it's definitely one-upped

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.320
Bloodborne graphically, in my opinion,

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.100
and see that over there? 
That's the new Firelink Shrine

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:26.840
and guarding it is: Iudex Gundyr, 
"The Ashen Judge".

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:34.360
Within his chest is the coiled sword, this sword is only bequeathed to chosen ash as judged by the

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.660
Iudex who awaits the arrival of ashes
as

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:41.760
and to quote another item description his back

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.570
has become a growing seedbed for
darkness, it doesn't feel right to commentate

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.570
this first fight, so enjoy.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:35.570
Did you see what happened at the end there? That little moment where I checked for arrows threw me

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:41.810
off so much it stopped me dodging and I think it stopped me killing him too. Good fight though, right?

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.300
I was pretty on point with my
parries but that dagger made the fight really tough

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.500
didn't do so well with my parries in the second fight

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.060
I've got to admire this guy's move set and animations though.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.810
In my final
fight I remember that this black tar

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.810
monster is pretty susceptible to fire.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:10.180
Before we get into Firelink Shrine get a
loaded injured over here, this guy its an

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:15.760
absolute bastard you've thought the last boss was tough? Try fighting this naked dude

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:21.960
with a katana, whether it be the stun locking, my inability to parry him three times,

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:28.440
his god-like ability to parry
me? but after about eight deaths I found

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:35.440
his, well our weakness "gravity" now a lot of people are going to stubbornly kill

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:41.110
this guy like I did but a katana class
weapon this early on is a pretty sweet

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:45.690
reward and compared to bloodborne I can
confirm that this game is great at

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:50.820
giving you a lot of weapons in the early
game I had access to over 30 in the

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:56.790
first three hours which is awesome and
finally let's get into firelink shrine and

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:01.700
as we enter pay special attention to the
music I love how it intertwined with the

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:05.520
dialogue of the characters and the tone
it lends to this place.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:04.640
The lords of cinder awoke but turned
their backs on their thrones and their

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.640
duty, it's our job to bring them back.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:42.500
I got so nostalgic when i saw Andre at the end of this tunnel

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.380
I ran straight pass one of the hags from the Dark souls 2 and

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:50.660
went to talk to
our old blacksmith from Dark Souls 1

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:34.580
The blacksmith fulfills really familiar tasks plus the
ability to choose how many of each Estus Flask you'd like

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:10.260
The torch is the most appropriate thing to buy here for now but, I am definitely buying that key that

00:09:10.269 --> 00:09:16.649
requires 20K souls. The handmaiden
also extends her wares when you bring her ash.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:22.259
Ashes are the remains of Heroes you find
on your journey and the new items she

00:09:22.259 --> 00:09:25.799
gets pertained to the type of ash that
you bring.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:38.280
So the thrones belong to the Lords of
Cinder who abandoned them and very

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.520
fittingly they all seem to resemble
gravestones

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:47.400
for to sit upon them means sacrificing
yourself to link the fire.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:53.240
Yhorm the Giant of the Profaned capital, the largest
throne of course.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:59.560
Farron's Undead Legion "The Abyss Watchers", you can see their swords leated upon their throne.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:03.520
Holy King Lothric, Last hope of his Line.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:08.080
Aldrich "Saint of the Deep", you can see the almost

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:13.130
plastic-like covering around it
protecting it from his body and finally

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:18.730
Ludlef the Exiled who apparently still
remains on his throne

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:35.200
Leveling up remains much the same, but there's the addition of

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:41.410
the luck stat which makes a return from
Demon Souls. Luck increases item drop

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:47.180
rates as well as a few other minor
things probably and while we level up the

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.500
firekeeper is chanting something

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:53.740
Let these souls withdrawn from their vessels,

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.120
manifestations of disparity,

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:02.300
elucidated by fire burrow deep within me,

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:07.080
retreating to a darkness beyond the reach of flame,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.920
Let them assume a new master, inhabiting in ash,

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.940
casting themselves upon new forms.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:31.460
The mark of Ash will guide thee to the land of the Lords, to Lothric

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.529
where the homes of the Lords converge

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:41.360
so that was Firelink our new home for Dark Souls 3
and unlike in previous Dark Souls

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:46.339
games it doesn't seem to be connected to
the rest of the world so the closest

00:12:46.339 --> 00:12:51.680
comparison to this hub will be Demon
Souls since that game had a disconnected

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:58.170
hub that you send in NPC's back to
but to me the strongest part of Dark Souls

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:05.300
was it's intertwined interconnected
world and areas including the hub so if

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.749
this is a step away from that, then I'm
honestly a little bit disappointed

00:13:09.749 --> 00:13:15.370
because the ability to walk to every
checkpoint from a disconnected hub is

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:21.480
definitely going to affect exploration
and world design regardless though time

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:26.639
will tell if this is a problem or not
and once again we find our way through

00:13:26.639 --> 00:13:32.009
the High Wall of Lothric where the
homes of the Lord of Cinder converge and

00:13:32.009 --> 00:13:35.990
most of you have seen this area but
there are some new things, for example

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:42.360
all the enemies now drop items and since
I chose the gold coins as my gift i

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:48.040
ended up being able to increase my luck
and i got really, really lucky with my drops,

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:51.699
I'm gonna come right out and say
it out of all the footage that comes out

00:13:51.699 --> 00:13:55.889
of this event on March 1st I reckon we
end up with the most fashionable

00:13:55.889 --> 00:14:01.790
character consider that a challenge to
the other uploaders, I guess? And of

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:07.050
course since all these items dropped for
me I can teach us a lot about the Lothric Knights

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:11.540
these Knights of Lothric
with their Drake's once crushed anything

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:17.279
that threaten their shores of course that
was a long long time ago the knight has

00:14:17.279 --> 00:14:22.290
served as one of the three pillars since
ancient times and shares place alongside the Wyverns

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:27.360
as a symbol of Lothric
on the flip side though the Lothric

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:33.749
knights are also said to have contended
with the dragons and their shields have

00:14:33.749 --> 00:14:37.991
lightning resistance which is befitting
of a dragon slayers arms

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.570
their crossbows are also blessed with the
power of lightning in anticipation of

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:48.670
the use of lightning bolts which we know
are effective against dragons so they

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:54.490
fight with and against dragons and the
Lightning Urn explains this to us it tells

00:14:54.490 --> 00:15:01.260
us that "The Knights of Lothric have since tamed 
dragons but were once hunters of dragons"

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:07.580
and finally they worshipped the Sun so
many connections here between Lothric

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:13.710
the land of the Lords, lightning, Sun,
Gwyn it's all here as we enter Lothric

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:19.410
castle we expect the dancer of the
Frigid Valley but now in her place is

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:25.610
Emma who sits beneath a restricted ladder
leading deeper into Lothric Castle

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.810
A castle rumored to devour men.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:16:02.140
Forge on through the great gate and raise this banner to proceed

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:13.940
this farewell gift is for you it is the insignia
of an old Covenant if you feel trespassers

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:31.560
Covenants are now changed belong the fly, which is great

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:35.320
there's an inventory slot that holds
your allegiance

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:47.940
go through the great gate and raise this
banner to proceed but beware the dog

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:53.900
keeps a close eye on things, the vile watchdog of the Boreal Valley

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:37.320
In episode two we face off against the
vile watchdog and we find an old friend in a

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:41.740
town I can't wait to show you guys that,
it's gonna be amazing I don't usually

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:46.850
ask this but if you could leave a like
that would be so fantastic I really want

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:52.280
this series to do well and this series
is going to get better come March 24th

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:56.470
when the Japanese version comes out
because I won't have time restrictions

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:00.740
on the amount of content I can upload so
we'll be able to go more in depth on so

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:03.990
many of the interesting things that I
had to cut out of this series in the

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:08.330
name of time restrictions you guys have
no idea how hard it is to cut down like

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:14.110
six hours of footage to a mere 45
minutes or so that's been really tough

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:19.890
and also having the full game on March
24th means I'll be able to record at my

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:25.450
own pace not just in one big sitting so the
production value will go up and I just

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.260
want to say thank you for supporting
this series, thank you for watching,

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:31.890
thanks for being patrons if you are and I'll see you in the next one

